[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One devenv task renders a root: export, view-check, wireline, render

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-TASK
TITLE: One devenv task renders a root: export, view-check, wireline, render
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
devenv tasks run --mode before view:render -- --root UID runs the strictdoc
export into a clean directory, the view check, the wireline and the
renderer, and leaves the page and the payload under output/view/, which is
gitignored: the canon is the source and the page is regenerable. Flipping
the view is passing a different root. The published artifact is a copy of
that page, republished by hand or by a task, never edited.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The task is the only sanctioned way to regenerate (the repo's generate:* convention); a page nobody can regenerate is the one-off render again.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-VIEWS-ARE-REGENERABLE
  ROLE: Governed_By
